Цитирует @SebastienBubeck: As part of the October 6 release we had a particularly clean advance on the matrix multiplication exponent, with a new upper bound of 9/4. Since then, the model has been working on a LOWER BOUND for this exponent. This is already pretty crazy since NOTHING was known for lower bounds! Today we announced that actually 9/4 is tight ... This is really the kind of result that I never thought I would see in my lifetime.

(btw, by an "old" result of Yin Tat Lee and collaborators this also implies that linear programs can be solved in time n^{9/4}.)

